# Peer — names of the environment variables the web app reads. Values live in
# .env.local, which is never committed. Provider keys are entered by each reader
# in the app, not here.

# Optional. Unset or anything other than "tiered" runs beta's single-plan
# mode: every signed-in reader is treated as paid, capped only by the shared
# daily breaker. Set to exactly "tiered" (after beta ends) to restore the
# free/trial/paid split built in ABC-freemium rounds 1-9 — a live trial stays
# a trial, an expired one drops to free, and each plan gets its own deep-report
# budget again. See entitlementMode() in src/lib/entitlement/resolve.ts.
PEER_ENTITLEMENT_MODE=

# Full-text discovery. Unpaywall and OpenAlex ask for a contact address on every
# request; without one the Unpaywall lookup is skipped and OpenAlex is called
# unidentified. Set to your own address.
UNPAYWALL_EMAIL=
OPENALEX_EMAIL=

# P2-S4a — optional. Every OpenAlex call this app makes (lexical search,
# affiliation/citation-neighborhood discovery, semantic search, topic/field
# exploration) sends this as `Authorization: Bearer <key>` when set — never
# as a URL parameter, so it can't leak into a logged URL. Unset (the
# default): every request is sent unkeyed, exactly as before this existed.
# Whether OpenAlex now requires a key for keyless access is unverified as of
# this writing (ABC-JEV-INTEGRATION.md §1p.B(3)) — this is safe to leave
# unset either way.
OPENALEX_API_KEY=

# P2-S4a — server-only, default off, independent of each other and of every
# other flag in this file. Only the literal value "on" enables either one;
# anything else (unset, "true", "1", a typo) keeps today's behavior exactly.
# Never settable from a request body — a client can never turn these on.
#
# PEER_CHANNEL_OPENALEX_SEMANTIC adds one OpenAlex semantic-search call
# per feed build (project-first query text, results tagged "semantic" so
# they can survive the literal-topic gate like citation-neighborhood
# candidates already do).
#
# PEER_CHANNEL_OPENALEX_TOPIC adds a small, bounded OpenAlex topic/field
# exploration call, tagged "topic-field". It now reads real topic ids at
# request time from the reader's own liked/saved-paper history (added by
# P2-S4c+d, see topPositiveOpenAlexTopicIds() in
# src/lib/preferences/topic-seeds.ts) -- turning it on is no longer a
# guaranteed no-op. As with the 3 positive-seed channels below, the
# precondition in docs/JEV-RELEASE-READINESS.md §2 Group A4 is now VERIFIED
# (P5-S4) -- still off by default pending a rollout decision, not pending
# review.
PEER_CHANNEL_OPENALEX_SEMANTIC=
PEER_CHANNEL_OPENALEX_TOPIC=

# P2-S4b — positive-seed channels: papers "like the ones you already
# saved". Server-only, default off, same "on"-only / never-from-a-request
# convention as the two flags just above. A signed-in owner's recent
# explicit positive feedback (Save, "More like this" — the most recent 10)
# is resolved server-side ONLY when at least one of these three is "on";
# a signed-out reader never triggers this regardless of these flags.
# Sending a reader's saved-paper ids to Semantic Scholar discloses their
# research interests to that provider, so PEER_CHANNEL_S2_RECOMMENDATIONS
# specifically stays off until the user explicitly authorizes live use
# (ABC-JEV-INTEGRATION.md §1o.5/§1p.B(5)) — fixtures/tests only until then.
#
# PEER_CHANNEL_S2_RECOMMENDATIONS calls Semantic Scholar's recommendations
# endpoint seeded with the owner's saved S2 paper ids, tagged "positive-seed".
#
# PEER_CHANNEL_OPENALEX_SEED_SIMILARITY calls OpenAlex semantic search
# seeded with each saved paper's own title (one call per seed, small cap),
# tagged "positive-seed".
#
# PEER_CHANNEL_POSITIVE_SEED_CITATIONS pulls the citation neighborhood of
# the owner's saved OpenAlex works (same mechanism the existing
# advisor-affiliation channel uses, seeded with the OWNER's own papers
# instead), tagged "citation".
#
# Every channel self-excludes: a paper the owner already saved is never
# returned as its own "new" recommendation. A paper id that appears in both
# the owner's positive AND negative feedback is now sent as neither (closed
# gap, P2-S4c+d). The per-owner daily cache precondition in
# docs/JEV-RELEASE-READINESS.md §2 Group A4 is now VERIFIED (P5-S4), including
# its outage-handling behavior -- these three still default off pending a
# rollout decision, not pending review.
PEER_CHANNEL_S2_RECOMMENDATIONS=
PEER_CHANNEL_OPENALEX_SEED_SIMILARITY=
PEER_CHANNEL_POSITIVE_SEED_CITATIONS=

# P2-S6 — hybrid retrieval ranking (RRF): blends the different search
# channels' own orderings into one fused ranking instead of relying on any
# single channel's order alone. Server-only, default off (today's ranking
# is unaffected). Only the literal value "on" enables it; anything else
# (unset, "true", "1", a typo) keeps today's behavior exactly. Never
# settable from a request body. See rankFusionEnabled() in
# src/lib/feed/pipeline.ts. The two accuracy gaps review found in the
# flag-on path are now fixed and independently verified; still do NOT
# enable in production yet -- a separate, deliberate evaluation sign-off
# is the remaining gate; see docs/JEV-RELEASE-READINESS.md §2 Group A6.
PEER_RANK_FUSION=

# Optional: the Python interpreter for the PDF text extractor, when it is not
# `python3` on PATH. A deployment with no interpreter reads no PDFs and says so.
PYTHON_BIN=

# Hosted PDFs: disabled unless explicitly enabled with a private durable volume
# OUTSIDE the served application directory. See docs/PRIVATE_PDF_UPLOADS.md.
# Use an encrypted volume, an authenticated deployment, and a daily call to
# /api/jobs/purge-uploads with Authorization: Bearer <CRON_SECRET>.
PEER_UPLOADS_ENABLED=false
PEER_PRIVATE_UPLOAD_DIR=

# 9-18: the bearer /api/jobs/purge-uploads and web/scripts/purge-uploads.mjs
# both require. On Vercel, set this in the project's environment variables —
# Vercel's own cron caller (repo-root vercel.json) then sends it
# automatically, nothing else to wire up. Self-hosting: set it here (or in
# the shell that runs `npm run purge-uploads`) and call that script on your
# own OS-level scheduler; nothing in this repo runs it for you. Never commit
# a real value.
CRON_SECRET=

# P4-S2 — owner-level dashboard delivery ledger (never lets a signed-in
# reader see a paper the server already delivered). Server-only, default
# off: leave unset until AFTER the dashboard_deliveries/dashboard_batches
# migration (web/supabase/migrations/20260924000000_dashboard_delivery_ledger.sql)
# has actually been applied — turning this on is the explicit rollout step,
# not a default. Only the literal value "on" enables it; anything else
# (unset, "false", "1", a typo) keeps today's behavior exactly. Never
# touches the email/scheduled-digest path, which has its own separate
# delivery history. HARD THRESHOLD before ever launching with this flag
# left off in production (today's real, default path): an "unattributed
# pending delivery" reconcile must be built first — see
# docs/JEV-RELEASE-READINESS.md §2 Group A1.
PEER_DASHBOARD_LEDGER=

# Digest send-window dedupe: extends the "did I already send this owner a
# briefing today" check from a rolling 6-hour window to a per-local-day
# check, backed by its own migration
# (web/supabase/migrations/20260924000300_briefing_deliveries_dedupe.sql).
# Server-only, default off (keeps today's 6-hour-window check). Only the
# literal value "on" enables it; anything else (unset, "true", "1", a typo)
# keeps today's behavior exactly. Leave unset until AFTER that migration has
# actually been applied, same rule as PEER_DASHBOARD_LEDGER above. See
# isDigestDedupeEnabled() in src/app/api/jobs/dispatch-digests/route.ts.
PEER_DIGEST_DEDUPE=

# TRIGGER-A — master switch for the prepare-ahead worker (has a reader's
# dashboard results ready a bit before their usual reading time). Server-
# only, default off. Only the literal value "on" enables it; anything else
# (unset, "true", "1", a typo) keeps today's behavior exactly (nothing
# scheduled, nothing built). Precondition chain, in order: (1) the
# dashboard_prepare_jobs migration
# (web/supabase/migrations/20260924000600_dashboard_prepare_jobs.sql) has
# actually been applied; (2) PEER_DASHBOARD_LEDGER above is ALSO "on" —
# enforced in code, not just here: with the ledger off, a prepared result
# would sit somewhere a real visit never looks, so this flag is a truthful
# no-op ("ledger_disabled") until the ledger flag is on too, never a silent
# waste of work. See GET /api/jobs/prepare-dashboards,
# web/src/app/api/jobs/prepare-dashboards/route.ts.
PEER_DASHBOARD_PREPARE=

# TRIGGER-A — retries a digest email that was claimed but never confirmed
# sent (e.g. the process died mid-send). Server-only, default off. Only the
# literal value "on" enables it; anything else keeps today's behavior
# exactly. Depends on PEER_DIGEST_DEDUPE above ALSO being "on" — enforced in
# code: no `payload.email` attempt records exist to retry until the dedupe
# claim path is on, so this is a structural no-op without it. IMPORTANT:
# this only retries a SEND — it does not make email reachable. Nobody can
# turn email on for their own account from the app today (the UI control
# was intentionally removed), so in practice this flag currently has
# nothing to retry either, until that separately returns. See
# GET /api/jobs/prepare-dashboards,
# web/src/app/api/jobs/prepare-dashboards/route.ts.
PEER_DIGEST_EMAIL_RETRY=

# P3-S4 — the master switch for the Jev broker PATH (separate from
# PEER_JEV_SHADOW below: this one says "the broker may be called at all";
# PEER_JEV_SHADOW says "route.ts may additionally schedule a background
# call after a response is sent" — both must be "on" before anything
# actually calls the broker). Server-only, default off. Only the literal
# value "on" enables it; anything else (unset, "true", "1", a typo) keeps
# today's behavior exactly. Never settable from a request body, never
# NEXT_PUBLIC_. See jevBrokerEnabled() in src/lib/decisions/broker-client.ts.
# Nothing in production calls the broker yet even when this is "on." The
# real Jev provider key (JEV_API_KEY) must NEVER be set anywhere in web/ —
# it lives only as a Supabase Edge Function secret, read solely inside
# web/supabase/functions/jev-broker/.
PEER_JEV_BROKER=

# P3-S5 — the Jev shadow: background-only, evaluation-only decision calls
# scheduled after a paper feed response is already sent (never inside the
# request, never affecting what a reader sees). Server-only, default off.
# Only the literal value "on" enables it; anything else (unset, "true", "1",
# a typo) keeps today's behavior exactly. Also requires the separate
# PEER_JEV_BROKER="on" flag above, a signed-in entitled reader with their AI
# switch on, and the broker config below — see web/src/app/api/feed/route.ts.
# Recommend setting an explicit maxDuration on that route before enabling
# this — see docs/JEV-RELEASE-READINESS.md §1/§2 Group B7.
PEER_JEV_SHADOW=

# The Next server's own credential to ITS OWN Supabase Edge Function broker
# — NOT the Jev API key itself. The real Jev key is never read by anything
# in web/, in any runtime: it lives only as a Supabase Edge Function secret
# (see web/supabase/functions/jev-broker/). Missing or blank URL/secret
# leaves shadow mode "unconfigured": no reservation, no call, ever. Like
# every other server-only credential in this file, PEER_JEV_BROKER_SECRET
# must never be set as a NEXT_PUBLIC_ value — doing so would ship it to the
# browser bundle.
PEER_JEV_BROKER_URL=
PEER_JEV_BROKER_SECRET=

# Daily call-count ceilings for the Jev shadow (count-based, not a token/
# dollar estimate — ABC-JEV-INTEGRATION.md §1p.H(1)). Optional; an unset or
# non-numeric value falls back to the documented default rather than
# disabling shadow mode. Defaults: 50 per user per day, 2000 across every
# user per day.
PEER_JEV_PER_USER_DAILY_CAP=
PEER_JEV_GLOBAL_DAILY_CAP=

# P3-S6 — a bounded backup opinion from a second AI model, used ONLY inside
# the Jev shadow above (background-only, never changes what a reader sees)
# when Jev's own answer says a dimension is "unknown." Server-only, default
# off. Only the literal value "on" enables it; anything else (unset, "true",
# "1", a typo) keeps today's behavior exactly. Deliberately separate from
# PEER_JEV_SHADOW: the shadow can run with this still off, which is the
# only state reachable in production today — this feature is structurally
# inert regardless of this flag's value, because it only ever runs on a
# company-funded AI capability and nothing in this codebase mints or
# injects one yet (see docs/JEV-RELEASE-READINESS.md §2 Group B8). Never
# spends a reader's own key. See geminiFallbackEnabled() in
# src/lib/decisions/flag.ts.
PEER_JEV_GEMINI_FALLBACK=

# Daily call-count ceilings for the Gemini fallback above (count-based, same
# convention as the Jev caps above). PROPOSED defaults, not sourced from any
# vendor number — confirm before any live rollout. Optional; an unset or
# non-numeric value falls back to the documented default. Defaults: 10 per
# user per day, 200 across every user per day. A separate, non-configurable
# ceiling of at most 5 calls per shadow run always applies too (not an env
# var — a fixed value in code). See readGeminiFallbackConfig() in
# src/lib/decisions/flag.ts.
PEER_JEV_GEMINI_FALLBACK_PER_USER_DAILY_CAP=
PEER_JEV_GEMINI_FALLBACK_GLOBAL_DAILY_CAP=

# SPEND-CAP — the master switch for the shared daily dollar cap on Peer's
# company-funded AI calls (the system Gemini key; never a reader's own BYOK
# key). Server-only, default off. Only the literal value "on" enables it;
# anything else (unset, "true", "1", a typo) keeps today's behavior exactly —
# no config read, no counter call at all. Never settable from a request body.
# See companySpendCapEnabled() in src/lib/usage/company-budget.ts.
#
# FAILS CLOSED, so the activation order matters: apply the
# company_spend_budget migration -> enter at least the company_model_prices
# rows by hand in the Supabase dashboard (company_spend_caps rows are
# optional — safe built-in defaults apply when absent) -> only then set this
# to "on". Turning it on before any price rows exist makes every
# company-funded call refuse (visible as "breaker" rows in usage_events),
# because a call with no known price cannot be honestly estimated. See
# docs/JEV-RELEASE-READINESS.md's SPEND-CAP knob row for the full activation
# order and how to edit the numbers.
PEER_COMPANY_SPEND_CAP=
